 It opens diagonal lines for my light-squared bishop (f1) and my queen (d1)\n3. It's the most popular opening move in chess history, leading to sharp, tactical positions\n4. It allows for quick piece development and aggressive play\n5. It sets the tempo and puts immediate pressure on Black to respond to the central challenge\n\nAnswer: P: e2-e4"}
