c4** or **B: f1-b5** - Developing the bishop with tempo.\n\nThe key insight is that my knight on f7 is fantastically placed. **N: f7-e5** looks extremely strong as it:\n- Centralizes the knight on a dominant square\n- Attacks the knight on f6 and controls key squares\n- Maintains pressure on Black's position\n- Keeps options open for further attacks\n\nReason: N: f7-e5 places my knight on the most dominant central square, from where it controls critical squares (d7, f7, g6, d3, c4), attacks Black's knight on f6, and maintains maximum pressure on Black's cramped position. This move keeps all my tactical options alive while improving my piece coordination.\n\nAnswer: N: f7-e5"}
