N: d5-e7+, Black's king must move (likely to e8, f7, or g8), and I maintain pressure with my knight in an aggressive position deep in Black's territory.\n\nReason: N: d5-e7 delivers check to the Black king on f8, forcing Black to respond to the immediate threat. This gains tempo, improves my knight's position, and keeps Black on the defensive. The knight on e7 will be well-placed to continue the attack or control key squares. Given that Black's king is exposed and hasn't castled, applying immediate pressure with forcing moves is the strongest approach.\n\nAnswer: N: d5-e7"}
