s queen while improving my knight's position. This forces Black to respond to the threat, giving me the initiative.\n\nReason: The knight move to d5 serves multiple purposes:\n1. It attacks the Black queen on b6, forcing it to relocate\n2. It centralizes my best piece on an excellent outpost\n3. It maintains pressure while improving my position\n4. It keeps tactical options open against Black's exposed king\n\nThis is clearly the most forcing and strategically sound continuation.\n\nAnswer: N: e7-d5"}
