ss immediate safety concerns.\n\n5. **N: f5-h4**: Attacks the Queen, forcing it to move, but my King safety is still paramount.\n\nReason: King safety is the foundation of any chess position. With my King still on e1 and Black having an active Queen on h6, I'm extremely vulnerable to tactical shots. Castling kingside (K: e1-g1) solves multiple problems: it moves my King to safety behind pawns, connects my Rooks, and activates the h1 Rook. This is a fundamental principle - before launching attacks, ensure your own King is secure.\n\nAnswer: K: e1-g1"}
