ate immediate threats.\n\n5. **N: f5-h4** - Attacks the queen, forcing it to move, but less effective than the fork.\n\nReason: N: f5-g7 is a royal fork - it checks the king on h8 while simultaneously attacking the queen on h6. Black must respond to the check by moving the king (the only legal move would be moving the king), and then I capture the queen on the next move. This wins Black's most powerful piece and gives me a decisive material advantage.\n\nAnswer: N: f5-g7"}
