h rank position.\n\nReason: \nR: e7-e8+ is the strongest move because:\n- It forces the Black king to move (likely Kg7 or Ke7)\n- Maintains the rook's activity on the back rank\n- Puts immediate pressure on Black's position\n- Keeps the initiative and prevents Black from coordinating their pieces\n- After the king moves, White can continue to dominate with the active rook\n\nAnswer: R: e7-e8"}
