ack this pawn from behind, which is the classical way to stop passed pawns. This move puts maximum pressure on Black's most advanced threat while keeping my Rook active. After Rb1, Black cannot easily advance the b3 pawn, and I can then coordinate my King and Rook to deal with other threats.\n\nAnswer: R: h1-b1"}
