ed pawn threat on the kingside. This forces Black's king to respond to my advancing pawns while I have numerical superiority (4 vs 1 pawns). Even if Black's a-pawn advances, I can create faster threats with multiple connected pawns supported by my nearby king.\n\nAnswer: P: g2-g4"}
