ncing to f6-f7-f8\n- Forces Black's king to respond to this threat rather than freely attacking my queenside pawns\n- Maintains the initiative - in pawn endgames, tempo is crucial\n- If Black's king goes to stop the f-pawn, my king can potentially support my queenside pawns or help the f-pawn\n- This is the most forcing move that puts maximum pressure on my opponent\n\nAnswer: P: f4-f5"}
